from pydantic.dataclasses import dataclass", "explanation": "Add the ConfigDict import needed for the v2 config replacement."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/geo.py:9:test-failure"], "search": "class StrictConfig:
    anystr_strip_whitespace = True
    validate_assignment = True", "replace": "StrictConfig = ConfigDict(
    str_strip_whitespace=True,
    validate_assignment=True,
)", "explanation": "Pydantic V2 deprecates class-based `config` in favor of ConfigDict (Pydantic V2 Migration Guide, https://errors.pydantic.dev/2.14/migration/). The v1 key `anystr_strip_whitespace` is renamed to `str_strip_whitespace` in v2 so the whitespace-stripping behavior is preserved. The decorator call `@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)` is already valid with a dict-based config and is left unchanged."}], "notes": "Fixed the reported finding by replacing the class-based config with a ConfigDict and renaming the v1 key anystr_strip_whitespace to v2's str_strip_whitespace so whitespace stripping is preserved. The decorator line itself needs no change because pydantic.dataclasses.dataclass accepts a ConfigDict via config=. Not changed, but worth a look: Point defines __post_init_post_parse__, a v1-only hook. Pydantic v2 dataclasses call __post_init__ instead, so the coordinate range check and label.title() may not run under v2. This is not part of the listed findings, so I left it alone; it should be verified by the tests (tests.test_geo) and, if confirmed, renamed to __post_init__ in a follow-up."}
